Carried patch, Windows only: link Palace's tests against zlib after MFEM.

test/unit/CMakeLists.txt links unit-tests to ZLIB::ZLIB directly, for the
boundary-viz test that decodes MFEM's compressed VTU output. libpalace already
links ZLIB::ZLIB PUBLIC, after MFEM, and the test target is in a subdirectory
of libpalace's, so it inherits both the headers and the library. The direct
link only moves zlib earlier: CMake emits it before libpalace's interface,
and so before libmfem.a. With a static MFEM (BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF, as on
Windows), found by find_library as a bare archive that records nothing it
needs, the test link then fails with undefined compress2 and compressBound
from MFEM's vtk.cpp. palace.exe links in libpalace's order and never noticed.
Here the test links zlib itself only when libpalace has not. Shared builds
link as before; not specific to Windows.

diff --git a/test/unit/CMakeLists.txt b/test/unit/CMakeLists.txt
index 5ff5ad5..59b5e0a 100644
--- a/test/unit/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/test/unit/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -81,10 +81,13 @@ target_link_libraries(unit-tests
           )
 
 # The PostOperator boundary-viz regression decodes MFEM's compressed binary VTU output
-# when MFEM is built with zlib support.
-find_package(ZLIB QUIET)
-if(ZLIB_FOUND)
-  target_link_libraries(unit-tests PRIVATE ZLIB::ZLIB)
+# when MFEM is built with zlib support. libpalace already links ZLIB::ZLIB PUBLIC, after
+# MFEM. A direct link here would put zlib before a static libmfem.a on the link line.
+if(NOT TARGET ZLIB::ZLIB)
+  find_package(ZLIB QUIET)
+  if(ZLIB_FOUND)
+    target_link_libraries(unit-tests PRIVATE ZLIB::ZLIB)
+  endif()
 endif()
 
 # Handle device source code
